    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.11_base_commutative_diagram.chapters.12_worked_counterexamples_avogadro.sections.02_avogadro_walkthrough.concrete_anchor_17_PathLawceqra#pathlaw_c_eq_r_a" .
silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_12_worked_counterexamples_avogadro_sections_02_avogadro_walkthrough_concrete_anchor_17_PathLawceqra#pathlaw_c_eq_r_a silm:hasLongDescription "The PathLaw_c_eq_r_a is the commuting path equation: Cat anchor equals refinement composed with DomesticCat-Cat embedding r. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'PathLaw_c_eq_r_a', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
